[h1]Overview[/h1]
Sixteen extra mask shapes for NANAME Floors, covering triangles, quarter squares, rounded corners and a centred diamond.

Each shape rotates in four directions, with mirrored versions included where rotation can't produce them. Every shape also includes its negative, so you can paint either split without having to swap which floor is laid down first.

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3293767181]NANAME Floors[/url] by [url=https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198322678771]LS[/url]
[*]Harmony (required by the base mod)
[/list]

Supports the same versions as the base mod - 1.4, 1.5 and 1.6.

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
This mod is add-on terrain masks and labels, nothing else. There's no code for anything to conflict with. Just load it after the base mod.

The shapes blend whichever two terrains you pick, which means floors from any other mod should work.

Adding sixteen extra shapes can crowd the picker, but the base mod has a settings section that lets you switch off any you don't use, including these.

[h1]Attention[/h1]
Safe to add to an existing save.

Removing it mid-save will break/remove any floors built with these shapes. Floors built with the base mod aren't affected.

This mod also relabels two masks belonging to NANAME Floors. Its quarter triangle covers an eighth of a tile, so that shape and its negative are labelled as [i]eighth triangle[/i] in the settings page aligned with how this mod has named them. The masks themselves are unchanged.

[h1]Source[/h1]
[url=https://github.com/arrisar/naname-floors]github.com/arrisar/naname-floors[/url]

Additional translations and new shapes are welcome as requests or PRs, I will do my best to accommodate or review anything as soon as I can.

[h1]Bug Reports[/h1]
Most bugs should be reported to the original mod as this one just adds additional shapes. If you do want to post them for me, feel free to post them to either the comments on this page, or open an Issue on GitHub.
